        "original_id": "cfab45a5-ed54-58a8-9f53-7c5353f8a00d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Larry Hagman, Nagisa Oshima\n- Roles: actor, director, producer, screenwriter\n- Works: Dallas, I Dream of Jeannie, In the Realm of the Senses, Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence, Gohatto\n- Topics: film, television, Japanese cinema\n\nFacts:\n- Larry Hagman was born on September 21, 1931, and became an American film and television actor, director, and producer.\n- Nagisa Oshima was born on March 31, 1932, and became a Japanese film director and screenwriter.\n- Larry Hagman was best known for playing Major Anthony \"Tony\" Nelson in the 1960s sitcom I Dream of Jeannie.\n- Nagisa Oshima directed In the Realm of the Senses, a 1976 sexually explicit film set in 1930s Japan.\n- Larry Hagman was also best known for playing J.R. Ewing in the 1980s primetime television soap opera Dallas.\n- Nagisa Oshima directed Merry Christmas, Mr. Lawrence, a 1983 film about Japanese World War II prisoners of war.\n- Nagisa Oshima directed the 1999 Japanese film Gohatto, also known as Taboo.\n- Larry Hagman died on November 23, 2012.\n- Nagisa Oshima died on January 15, 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
